<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_CrecheMarker.xml                   UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M6 build pass (miasma_kit_spec.md M6, "Warden mothers
  and the crèches"). The "named area marker" the spec calls out by name:
  "a RUT_CrecheMarker invisible building holding the site identity; gives
  the 'mapped and named' ground." Placed by RM_SetPieceElement_SpawnMarker
  (RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards), one per site, via
  RUT_GenStep_CrecheScatterer (Defs/MapGeneration/RUT_Miasma_CrecheScatterer.xml).

  Genuinely invisible, not "awaiting art": drawerType None + no graphicData
  at all, same shape as this mod's own RM_Dunes_BuriedCache.xml precedent
  ("a texPath that does not resolve renders nothing and reports nothing,
  which is the exact silent failure this mod's whole discipline is
  against" — so this def names no texture rather than a fake one). This is
  the correct end state, not a placeholder: the spec's own text calls it
  "invisible."

  Not player-placeable (map-gen only): no designationCategory, no costList,
  no constructEffect — ParentName="BuildingBase" is used only for the
  Building-category defaults (altitudeLayer, tickerType shape), same as
  BuriedCache's own reasoning for its own parent choice, not because this
  is meant to be built.

  destroyable false + useHitPoints false: this is map STATE, not a prop a
  raid or a mishap can casually erase — the despoiled-memory mechanic
  (RM_CompCrecheMarker) is keyed on the WARDEN pawn's death, never on the
  marker's own, so a marker that could be destroyed independently would
  let a player dodge the memory mechanic entirely by demolishing it. This
  mirrors ThingDef.ConfigErrors' own flammability/useHitPoints pairing
  BuriedCache's own header already flags — Flammability 0 avoids that trap
  here too.

  selectable true (unlike BuriedCache) so RM_CompCrecheMarker.
  CompInspectStringExtra's despoiled/intact line is actually visible to a
  player who clicks the crèche shallows — "mapped and named" ground should
  read as inspectable, not merely present.

  despoiledManhunterFactorDurationDays 10 / despoiledManhunterChanceFactor
  1.5 are the spec's own INVENTED M6 §8 values, passed straight through
  ("manhunter-chance factor x1.5 for 10 days — a factor, not an event").

  Translation keys RUT_CrecheMarkerDespoiled/RUT_CrecheMarkerIntact are
  referenced by RM_CompCrecheMarker.CompInspectStringExtra but not yet
  added to a Languages/ folder — same owed shape this item's own M4/M5
  build passes already flagged for their own letter keys (.Translate()
  falls back to the raw key rather than erroring; does not block anything).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_CrecheMarker</defName>
    <label>crèche marker</label>
    <description>An unmarked stretch of brine shallows that the map itself remembers as a warden's nursery ground. Nothing here looks different to a stranger — the memory belongs to the site, not to anything built on it.</description>
    <thingClass>Building</thingClass>
    <category>Building</category>
    <drawerType>None</drawerType>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>Standable</passability>
    <fillPercent>0</fillPercent>
    <coversFloor>false</coversFloor>
    <size>(1,1)</size>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <useHitPoints>false</useHitPoints>
    <destroyable>false</destroyable>
    <neverMultiSelect>true</neverMultiSelect>
    <tickerType>Never</tickerType>
    <statBases>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Beauty>0</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompProperties_CrecheMarker">
        <despoiledManhunterFactorDurationDays>10</despoiledManhunterFactorDurationDays>
        <despoiledManhunterChanceFactor>1.5</despoiledManhunterChanceFactor>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
